{
  "slug": "js_date_methods",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 59,
  "url": "/js/js_date_methods.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript Get Date Methods",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Get Date Methods"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The new Date() Constructor"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In JavaScript, date objects are created with new Date()."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "new Date() returns a date object with the current date and time."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const date = new Date();",
      "caption": "Get the Current Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_new"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Date Get Methods"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Method", "Description"],
      "rows": [
        ["getFullYear()", "Get year as a four digit number (yyyy)"],
        ["getMonth()", "Get month as a number (0-11)"],
        ["getDate()", "Get day as a number (1-31)"],
        ["getDay()", "Get weekday as a number (0-6)"],
        ["getHours()", "Get hour (0-23)"],
        ["getMinutes()", "Get minute (0-59)"],
        ["getSeconds()", "Get second (0-59)"],
        ["getMilliseconds()", "Get millisecond (0-999)"],
        ["getTime()", "Get time (milliseconds since January 1, 1970)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The get methods above return Local time."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Universal time (UTC) is documented at the bottom of this page."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The get methods return information from existing date objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In a date object, the time is static. The \"clock\" is not \"running\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The time in a date object is NOT the same as current time."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getFullYear() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getFullYear() method returns the year of a date as a four digit number:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getFullYear();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getFullYear();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_getfullyear2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Warning !"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Old JavaScript code might use the non-standard method getYear()."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "getYear() is supposed to return a 2-digit year."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "getYear() is deprecated. Do not use it!"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getMonth() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getMonth() method returns the month of a date as a number (0-11)."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "In JavaScript, January is month number 0, February is number 1, ...\nFinally, December is month number 11."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getMonth();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getMonth();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_getmonth2"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "You can use an array of names to return the month as a name:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const months = [\"January\", \"February\", \"March\", \"April\", \"May\",\n\"June\", \"July\", \"August\", \"September\", \"October\",\n\"November\", \"December\"];\n\nconst d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nlet month = months[d.getMonth()];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const months = [\"January\", \"February\", \"March\", \"April\", \"May\",\n\"June\", \"July\", \"August\", \"September\", \"October\",\n\"November\", \"December\"];\n\nconst d = new Date();\n\nlet month = months[d.getMonth()];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_month2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getDate() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getDate() method returns the day of a date as a number (1-31):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getDate();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getDate();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_getdate2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getHours() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getHours() method returns the hours of a date as a number (0-23):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getHours();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getHours();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_gethours2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getMinutes() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getMinutes() method returns the minutes of a date as a number (0-59):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getMinutes();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getMinutes();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_getminutes2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getSeconds() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getSeconds() method returns the seconds of a date as a number (0-59):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getSeconds();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getSeconds();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_getseconds2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getMilliseconds() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getMilliseconds() method returns the milliseconds of a date as a number (0-999):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getMilliseconds();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getMilliseconds();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_getmilliseconds2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getDay() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getDay() method returns the weekday of a date as a number (0-6)."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "note",
      "text": "In JavaScript, the first day of the week (day 0) is Sunday.\nSome countries in the world consider the first day of the week to be Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getDay();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getDay();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_getday2"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can use an array of names, and getDay() to return weekday as a name:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const days = [\"Sunday\", \"Monday\", \"Tuesday\", \"Wednesday\",\n\"Thursday\", \"Friday\", \"Saturday\"];\n\nconst d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nlet day = days[d.getDay()];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const days = [\"Sunday\", \"Monday\", \"Tuesday\", \"Wednesday\",\n\"Thursday\", \"Friday\", \"Saturday\"];\n\nconst d = new Date();\n\nlet day = days[d.getDay()];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_weekday2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getTime() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getTime() method returns the number of milliseconds since January 1, 1970:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"1970-01-01\");\n\nd.getTime();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date(\"2021-03-25\");\n\nd.getTime();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const d = new Date();\n\nd.getTime();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_gettime3"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Date.now() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Date.now() returns the number of milliseconds since January 1, 1970."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let ms = Date.now();",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const minute = 1000 * 60;\n\nconst hour = minute * 60;\n\nconst day = hour * 24;\n\nconst year = day * 365;\n\nlet years = Math.round(Date.now() / year);",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_now"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Date.now() is a static method of the Date object."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You cannot use it on a date object like myDate.now()."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The syntax is always Date.now()."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "UTC Date Get Methods"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Method", "Same As", "Description"],
      "rows": [
        ["getUTCDate()", "getDate()", "Returns the UTC date"],
        ["getUTCFullYear()", "getFullYear()", "Returns the UTC year"],
        ["getUTCMonth()", "getMonth()", "Returns the UTC month"],
        ["getUTCDay()", "getDay()", "Returns the UTC day"],
        ["getUTCHours()", "getHours()", "Returns the UTC hour"],
        ["getUTCMinutes()", "getMinutes()", "Returns the UTC minutes"],
        ["getUTCSeconds()", "getSeconds()", "Returns the UTC seconds"],
        ["getUTCMilliseconds()", "getMilliseconds()", "Returns the UTC milliseconds"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "UTC methods use UTC time (Coordinated Universal Time)."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "UTC time is the same as GMT (Greenwich Mean Time)."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The difference between Local time and UTC time can be up to 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Local Time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "UTC Time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The getTimezoneOffset() Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The getTimezoneOffset() method returns the difference (in minutes)\nbetween local time an UTC time:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let diff = d.getTimezoneOffset();",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_date_gettimezoneoffset"
    },
